<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Starting research for "A House of Your Own" when Medieval Overhaul is loaded.

    The base scenario already grants the vanilla medieval foundation (Smithing, Stonecutting,
    Complex Clothing, Long Blades, Plate Armor, Brewing). Medieval Overhaul re-gates most
    everyday medieval crafting behind its own tree, so without this a House starts unable to
    make furniture, tan leather, cook properly or forge the simplest weapons - which is a
    harsher opening than vanilla, not a fairer one.

    Scope is deliberately the domestic tier only - the crafts a standing holdfast would already
    have, so the opening is not a grind. Arms and armour are NOT granted: those are the first
    things the campaign should make you earn.

      Lumber -> RusticFurniture          (furniture and storage)
      BasicCooking, BasicAgriculture      (a hall that can feed itself)
      LeatherTanning                      (hides)

    Withheld: Candle making, the Basic/Military/Noble weapon lines, Protective Clothing,
    Alchemy, Gunpowder, Steel, Plasteel, Engineering, Mining, Ballista and Trebuchet.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Medieval Overhaul</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/ScenarioDef[defName="ARIOIAF_HouseOfYourOwn"]/scenario/parts/li[@Class="ARimOfIceAndFire.Scenarios.ScenPart_ARIOIAF_StartingResearch"]/projects</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>DankPyon_Lumber</li>
        <li>DankPyon_RusticFurniture</li>
        <li>DankPyon_BasicCooking</li>
        <li>DankPyon_BasicAgriculture</li>
        <li>DankPyon_LeatherTanning</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
